      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need help writing a rejection email. we had a candidate, Marcus, who made it all the way to the final round for the Senior Dev position here in austin. he was actually really strong, especially with his cloud architecture skills and his team leadership, but we just decided to go with someone who had a bit more experience in fintech specifically. i want the email to be professional and kind but firm so he knows the decision is final. can u help me draft something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a draft for you:\n\n---\n\n**Subject: Update on Your Application – Senior Developer Position**\n\nDear Marcus,\n\nThank you for taking the time to interview for the Senior Developer position with our Austin team. We truly enjoyed getting to know you throughout the process.\n\nWe were consistently impressed by your cloud architecture expertise and leadership abilities, and this was a difficult decision. After careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with a candidate whose experience more closely aligns with our current needs, specifically in the fintech space. This was not an easy choice, and we want to acknowledge the strength of your candidacy.\n\nWe would like to keep your résumé on file and encourage you to apply for future openings that match your background. We wish you all the best in your job search and future career endeavors.\n\nSincerely,\n[Your Name]\n[Your Title]\n[Company Name]\n\n---\n\nA few notes: the final round phrasing signals the decision is conclusive without being harsh, and mentioning the specific strength (fintech experience gap) gives him honest closure without leaving the door open to negotiation. Feel free to tweak the tone or trim it down if you'd like something shorter.",
